dsv41 patch 0075 (22.10.2026): skip the decoder replay on intermediate prefill chunks. In use from image v24 (VLLM_DSV41_REPLAY_SKIP=1).

Switch: VLLM_DSV41_REPLAY_SKIP=1 (both sides, worker + scheduler; default 0 = v22 behaviour, bit for bit).
Base: image v22 (gh_stage/docker/files = v22: model_state.py = v0067/src, scheduler.py = v0074/src).

What: with SWA bounded replay (0034 / vLLM #59894), every eager prefill step runs layers 20-39 again on each request's
last 128 rows (layer 20 writes its KV for every row first). Layers 21-39 own only sliding-window KV, and a trimmed chunk
reads replay-layer window KV only from its own kept rows (kv_start = max(replay_start, seq_len - window)). So the
replay of an intermediate chunk is read by nothing if the next chunk trims too: no logits survive a partial prefill,
the DSpark drafter attends over 128 positions of its own context, decode reads only the last chunk's window.
The patch keeps ONE row (the chunk's last, window clamped to itself) for a prefill request whose chunk trims, leaves
more than a window (remaining_after > window) and is text only without prompt logprobs; the scheduler never gives a
text request with more than a window left a chunk of <= window rows (it waits a step; budget left <= 128 of 4096), so
the chunk after a skipped one always trims. Last chunk, decode window KV, final logits: unchanged.
Gain (estimate, GB10 TP2): ~0.1 s of ~1.9 s per intermediate 4096-token chunk (20 layers' MoE on 128 rows ~86 % of the
experts + 5 indexers over the context) -> prefill +5-7 % for prompts > 4,224 tokens, 0 bytes of memory.
Files: models/deepseek_v41/replay_skip.py (new, numpy only), nvidia/model_state.py (mask + kv_start clamp on the kept
length, identical for kept_len == window), v1/core/sched/scheduler.py (inline rule, 2 call sites).
Tests: loops/replay_skip/test_replay_skip.py (CPU: helpers, rule == helper, provenance simulation of the replay
layers' window KV over 3000 random requests / 14,226 chunks / 7,688 skipped replays: final output + decode window
identical; 4 mutations detected).

Measured (22.10.2026, images v23/v24, 2x GB10, spark2 at 2000 MHz unless noted, A/B on adjacent fresh starts):
  - needle prompt of 478,817 tokens: prefill 229.4 -> 218.7 s (+4.9 %, v23 window W2), 230.9 -> 218.1 s (+5.9 %, v24
    window W3, together with 0076/0077/0081); first window at 2190 MHz: 224.4 -> 213.3 s (+5.2 %);
  - 26K-token prompts: no gain (-0.6 to -2.8 %, within noise and the clock cap);
  - first answer token of 50K-token needle questions (p ~ 1): KL 0.0017 mean / 0.0025 max against the same image
    without the switch (two fresh computes: 0.0015 / 0.0037); T=0 short prompts 8/8 identical; memory unchanged.

